X13 — hot-path allocation in validate()
-----------------------------------------
`validate()` (`:101-113`) constructs a throwaway `DistannRowSchemaAttribute` per
attribute purely to call `fixed_binary_width(&schema_attribute)`. That
construction clones `type_namespace`, `type_name`, `collation_namespace`,
`collation_name`, `send_function`, `receive_function` and allocates
`"covered".to_owned()` — roughly five heap allocations per attribute per call
(the two collation clones are empty and do not allocate).

`validate()` is called by `encode()` (`:147`), `encode_payload()` (`:254`), and
`decode_payload()` (`:290`). So it runs once per encoded row and once per
decoded row. For the preregistered bench cover (`covering_payload_attnums='1'`,
one attribute) over a lazy-10 window that is ~50 allocations per window of pure
validation overhead; at the 16-attribute maximum it is ~800 per window.

`fixed_binary_width` (`:39-51`) reads only `type_namespace` and `type_name`, so
the whole construction is avoidable by changing its signature to
`fn fixed_binary_width(type_namespace: &str, type_name: &str) -> Option<u16>`.
Not a correctness defect and not on any measured path yet — but it sits
directly on the path whose PROMOTE gate is ">= 5.0% and >= 0.50 ms" at 100k
(plan 001 §6).


